# Line endings — one representation, every OS.
#
# This repo is developed from both Windows and Linux against the same working
# tree. Without this file git's per-machine `core.autocrlf` decides the on-disk
# form, so a checkout made on Windows shows up as "every file modified" the
# moment it is opened on Linux (36k phantom line changes across 76 files —
# measured, not hypothetical). Pinning eol=lf makes the working tree identical
# on both hosts; the repository blobs were already LF, so nothing is rewritten.
#
# Rust, git and every editor in use here read LF natively on Windows.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows-native scripts must keep CRLF: cmd.exe and older PowerShell hosts
# mis-parse LF-only batch files.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Binary — never touch, never diff as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.exe binary
*.dll binary
*.so binary
*.dylib binary
*.bin binary
*.dat binary

# Generated / vendored: keep them out of diff noise and language stats.
Cargo.lock -diff linguist-generated
archive/** linguist-vendored
